1. Open Windows Server Backup on your training VM and perform a one-time full backup of the C: drive. Take a screenshot of the confirmation screen after completion.
=>Open Server Manager → Tools → Windows Server Backup
(or run wbadmin.msc).
In the right Actions pane, click Backup Once….
Choose Different options → Next.
Select Custom → Next.
Click Add Items → select the C: volume (or the entire bare-metal / system state if you prefer a fuller recovery option) → OK → Next.
Choose the destination (local disk, volume, or network share) → Next.
Confirm the settings and click Backup.
Wait for the operation to finish. The final confirmation screen shows “Backup completed successfully” (or similar) with start/end time and status.

2. Configure a scheduled incremental backup in Windows Server Backup to run daily at 8:00 PM for the folder containing your music or video files (e.g., D:\Media). Document the steps you followed and the schedule settings you chose.
=>In Windows Server Backup, click Backup Schedule… in the Actions pane.
Choose Custom → Next.
Add Items → select the folder (e.g. D:\Media) → Next.
On the Specify Backup Time page:
Select Once a day.
Set the time to 20:00 (8:00 PM).
Choose the destination 
Confirm and finish the wizard. Windows Server Backup will create a scheduled task that runs daily.

